Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Privacy and attribution.",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " Live coordinates are coarsened to one decimal place (~11 km) before \
plotting or storage, so no precise observer or sensitive-species location is \
republished. All live data are attributed to eBird.org (Cornell Lab of \
Ornithology) per the eBird Terms of Use."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"da99815f-3fbc-4a57-8d80-ef4328612488"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["7.  What each journey reveals", "Section",
 FontFamily->"Roboto Condensed",
 FontSize->30,
 FontColor->RGBColor[
  0.153, 0.51, 0.64],ExpressionUUID->"ad27647c-b175-482b-85df-672dc35d6070"],

Cell["\<\
Read together, the three tracks tell three different stories about how a bird \
can solve the problem of seasonal survival.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"bb42e64a-2edf-4f46-b920-ff5896def208"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Arctic tern \[LongDash] the pole-to-pole Atlantic sweep.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " The latitude-versus-month signal is the cleanest in the dataset: a \
centroid that climbs to high-Arctic breeding latitudes in the boreal summer \
and plunges toward the Southern Ocean in the austral summer. The centroid \
displacement (~24,100 km) is large yet still understates the individual \
journey (~70,900 km), because circumpolar east\[Dash]west motion cancels in \
the population mean \[LongDash] a vivid illustration of the difference \
between a population statistic and an individual track."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"c66b81cd-8c33-4302-82d3-e5bde8ea41a0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Common swift \[LongDash] the Europe\[LeftRightArrow]sub-Saharan \
shuttle.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " A single coherent flyway, and therefore the easiest centroid to trust: a \
tight summer concentration over Europe collapses into a sub-Saharan African \
wintering centre and back, ~14,000 km of annual centroid travel. The swift \
shows what the method looks like when nothing has to be corrected for \
multiple populations \[LongDash] it just works."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"f0158ba0-9926-446a-97a5-18b77adef981"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Red knot \[LongDash] the Americas long-haul (and the cautionary \
tale).",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " On its Americas flyway the knot traces a coherent ~7,900 km loop between \
Arctic breeding grounds and southern wintering areas, with the Delaware Bay \
stopover embedded in the spring leg. It is also the species that exposed the \
multi-flyway trap: pooled globally, its centroid is nonsense. The knot is the \
reason this post insists on per-flyway analysis."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"57655222-8f5b-41c7-8d37-a853961c7784"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["8.  Conclusions", "Section",
 FontFamily->"Roboto Condensed",
 FontSize->30,
 FontColor->RGBColor[
  0.153, 0.51, 0.64],ExpressionUUID->"930a708d-6956-4621-9356-afbea428eed6"],

Cell["\<\
With open data and a careful method, you can reconstruct continental-scale \
bird migration from a laptop. Hundreds of millions of volunteer observations, \
republished under an open licence with a citable DOI, plus a few dozen lines \
of Wolfram Language, are enough to recover the annual journeys of three of \
the planet's great migrants and to cross-validate them against a professional \
abundance model.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"0805971a-98f6-4aeb-93f7-80c25421eefa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "But the central lesson is a cautionary one. ",
 StyleBox["Naive pooling misleads.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " A single global centroid placed the red knot in the empty mid-Atlantic, \
~4,670 km/month from any real bird. Two disciplines rescue the analysis: ",
 StyleBox["bias-awareness",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (presence weighting on a coarse grid, so birders are not mistaken for \
birds) and ",
 StyleBox["per-flyway analysis",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (so disjoint populations are never averaged together), all on a ",
 StyleBox["proper spherical geometry",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (so longitudes are never averaged arithmetically). Get those three right \
and citizen-science occurrence data yield a faithful, validated picture of \
where the birds actually are."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"0fd9f161-f74f-432b-bb11-55660e0bf562"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

